From b060b060e9fc3304214a79b449e3f9526e2740e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 21:32:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0328 -- skip fully-transparent BG tiles
 (byte-identical)

The real-hardware TBG1 census (patch 0327's MDS_TBG_INSTR) found that
93.4-93.6% of every BG tile actually drawn is tile-0 (empty), the pass is
cleanly count-bound (~41.5 us/tile flat), and skipping those blits
projects a 2.8-9.2 ms/tick saving -- enough to clear the Mach64 KPI gap.

Why this is a correctness-preserving speedup, not a gamble. Tilesets load
with the colorkey set to master palette index 0 (black) in wave-16
indexed mode, and _blit_indexed writes only pixels where px != colorkey.
So a tile whose every pixel is index 0 writes ZERO pixels today -- the
backdrop (drawn earlier in DrawScene) already shows through it. Skipping
such a blit is byte-identical to performing it, the same property patch
0130's occlusion table already relies on.

The skip is NOT a literal t==0 compare (that would assume tile index 0 is
blank in every tileset -- data-dependent, breakable by a mod). Instead
Tileset::_computeBlankTiles scans the loaded tilesheet once per map load
and marks every tile whose pixels are ALL the colorkey; the BG loop skips
exactly those. Safe-by-construction on any tileset -- it can only ever
skip blits that provably write nothing, and it correctly skips nothing
when a tileset has a non-blank tile-0 or no colorkey (or a non-INDEX8
surface). Mirrors drawTile's src-rect math so detection matches the blit.

Scope: BG pass only (foreground == 0, the measured win); the FG pass and
the default-OFF tilemap-cache fill path (patch 0132) are untouched. Only
the plain drawTile branch is gated -- TA_CURRENT / 0x43 special sprites
still draw.

Killswitch SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_BG_BLANK_SKIP (default ON, strict-0
disables). No killswitch is needed for correctness; it exists for A/B
ablation, a clean revert on the hottest render loop, and because the
non-default DRAWTILE_FAST=0 path records dirty rects (the default
drawTileFast does not) so the skip has a subtle dirty-rect interaction
there (argued benign -- pixels identical, region covered by the
backdrop's own draw -- but worth being able to revert).

Instrumentation: adds g_mds_tbg_tiles_skipped_blank to patch 0327's
census so visited == drawn_normal + drawn_special + skipped_attr +
skipped_oob + skipped_blank stays balanced, which also measures the
lever's engagement on hardware. Diag-gated (counts only under
MDS_TBG_INSTR=1). Per-load 'blank-tile precompute -- N of M ...' line +
an always-on initVideo banner are the two-witness hooks; the FG (tfg,
patch 0111) census is untouched.

docs/BOOT.md, CLRENV.BAT and the smoke BANNERS entry ride in the outer
repo.

